    {
      "id": "summary",
      "number": "11",
      "title": "Consolidated Design Summary",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "block": "prose",
          "text": "The analysed firmware is organized into application, board-support, configuration, interface, platform, and utility modules. At the hardware boundary, the recorded GPIOs are PA0 as an input and PD12 as an output. The brief identifies no tasks, so it does not establish what the runtime does on each cycle. No buses, network transports, or sinks are recorded as destinations for data leaving the device. The module separation and the two GPIO roles are established, but detailed runtime behavior and data contracts are not specified in the brief. No open decisions are recorded."
        },
